{"name":"Circus Peanut","hex":"#ad835c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"circus peanut","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A peanut-shaped flavored marshmallow candy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circus_peanut"}],"entries":[{"title":"Circus peanut","blocks":[{"text":"Circus peanuts are American peanut-shaped marshmallow candy. They date to the 19th century, when they were one of a large variety of unwrapped \"penny candy\" sold in such retail outlets as five-and-dime stores."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Orange-Circus-Peanuts.jpg/330px-Orange-Circus-Peanuts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circus_peanut","wikidata":"Q5121827"},{"title":"Circus","blocks":[{"text":"A circus is a company of performers who put on diverse entertainment shows that may include clowns, acrobats, trained animals, trapeze acts, musicians, dancers, hoopers, tightrope walkers, jugglers, magicians, ventriloquists, and unicyclists as well as other object manipulation and stunt-oriented artists. The term \"circus\" also describes the field of performance, training, and community which has followed various formats through its 250-year modern history."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Barnum_%26_Bailey_clowns_and_geese2.jpg/330px-Barnum_%26_Bailey_clowns_and_geese2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circus","wikidata":"Q47928"},{"title":"Peanut","blocks":[{"text":"The peanut, also known as the groundnut, goober, goober pea, pindar or monkey nut (UK), is a legume crop grown mainly for its edible seeds, contained in underground pods. It is widely grown in the tropics and subtropics by small and large commercial producers, both as a grain legume and as an oil crop. Underground fruiting (geocarpy) is atypical among legumes, which led botanist Carl Linnaeus to name the species hypogaea, from Greek 'under the earth'."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Arachis_hypogaea_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-163.jpg/330px-Arachis_hypogaea_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-163.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peanut","wikidata":"Q37383"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Champion_great_danes_from_the_Imperial_kennels%2C_poster_for_Forepaugh_and_Sells_Brothers%2C_1898.jpg/500px-Champion_great_danes_from_the_Imperial_kennels%2C_poster_for_Forepaugh_and_Sells_Brothers%2C_1898.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Champion_great_danes_from_the_Imperial_kennels%2C_poster_for_Forepaugh_and_Sells_Brothers%2C_1898.jpg/500px-Champion_great_danes_from_the_Imperial_kennels%2C_poster_for_Forepaugh_and_Sells_Brothers%2C_1898.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sells Brothers Circus with Great Danes ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChampion_great_danes_from_the_Imperial_kennels%2C_poster_for_Forepaugh_and_Sells_Brothers%2C_1898.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Astley%27s_Amphitheatre_Microcosm_edited.jpg/500px-Astley%27s_Amphitheatre_Microcosm_edited.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Astley%27s_Amphitheatre_Microcosm_edited.jpg/500px-Astley%27s_Amphitheatre_Microcosm_edited.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Astley's Amphitheatre in London, c. 1808","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAstley's_Amphitheatre_Microcosm_edited.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/c